           UTF8 string, which can be handled in diverse ways by other provided
           implementations.  The encoding of the object depends on the context
           it’s  used  in;  for  example,  OOSSSSLL__DDEECCOODDEERR(3)   allows   multiple
           encodings,  depending  on  existing  decoders.   If central OpenSSL
           library functionality is to handle the data directly,  it  mmuusstt  be
           encoded  in  DER  for  all object types except for OOSSSSLL__OOBBJJEECCTT__NNAAMMEE
           (see "Parameter reference" below), where it’s assumed  to  a  plain
           UTF8 string.

